<v NARRATOR>This drama uses an AI-generated voice. Voiced via Gemini 2.5.

3
00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:27.392
<v NARRATOR>In the dim, damp heart of a fallen log, a soft brown tumble of a creature was hard at work, sleeves dusty with dark rich soil.

4
00:00:27.392 --> 00:00:36.483
<v CRUMBLE>I am Crumble, and I am a decomposer — people think my work is destroying, but really it is returning.

5
00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:44.814
<v NARRATOR>Crumble lifted a fistful of sweet-smelling earth that had, not long ago, been a green leaf.

6
00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:54.105
<v CRUMBLE>A dead leaf is not garbage — it is a locked box of nutrients, and my enzymes are the key that opens it.

7
00:00:54.105 --> 00:01:03.556
<v CRUMBLE>I release tiny chemical scissors that cut the tough dead molecules into small simple ones the soil can hold again.

8
00:01:03.556 --> 00:01:11.327
<v NARRATOR>Crumble kept a little of the energy as a meal, and let the nitrogen and minerals dissolve free into the ground.

9
00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:22.138
<v CRUMBLE>That is why a forest never drowns in its own fallen leaves — every autumn's leaves become next spring's growth.

10
00:01:22.138 --> 00:01:32.909
<v NARRATOR>When Crumble was small, the fast bright creatures got all the praise, and the slow dissolving in the dark went unwatched.

11
00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:45.880
<v CRUMBLE>I once thought mine was the lowly job, until a patch of soil lost its decomposers and the leaves just piled and choked, and nothing new could root.

12
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:55.051
<v CRUMBLE>The bloom everyone praises is only possible because someone, unthanked, returned last year's bloom to the earth.

13
00:01:55.051 --> 00:02:00.942
<v NARRATOR>A student asked, a little disgusted, why anyone should care about rot.

14
00:02:00.942 --> 00:02:11.233
<v CRUMBLE>It is not rot the way you mean it — it is repair, keeping the same handful of matter moving from leaf to soil to root and back again.

15
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:22.484
<v NARRATOR>Nothing is wasted, and nothing is ever really thrown away. That is the great returning, and that is what makes Crumble Crumble.

16
